`--help` succeeds outside any project, names all seven flags, and enumerates the clause forms
`--where` accepts, including both ordering suffixes.

-- cmd --
booping query --help
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
usage: booping query [-h] [--config DOTTED.PATH] [--glob PATTERN]
                     [--where K=V] [--sort FIELD] [--columns A,B]
                     [--output FORMAT] [--project PATH]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --config DOTTED.PATH  Dotted path into the merged config whose value is the
                        query spec; mutually exclusive with --glob
  --glob PATTERN        Vault-relative glob to match; repeatable and ordered —
                        the first glob claiming a slug wins
  --where K=V           Filter clause: k=v, k!=v, k:in=a,b, k:gt=n or k:lt=n
                        (:gt / :lt compare numerically); repeatable, all
                        clauses apply
  --sort FIELD          Sort by this frontmatter field; '-' prefix for
                        descending
  --columns A,B         Comma-separated projection; declared order is
                        preserved
  --output FORMAT       Output format: table, json, yaml, paths (default:
                        table)
  --project PATH        Resolve context against this vault instead of the
                        attached project
-- stderr --
